Here's a summary of what was implemented:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mbuffer.rs[22m - Dynamic byte buffer with read/write/peek operations, auto-growing capacity. Returns [38;5;10m0xFF[0m char on EOF (matching C's [38;5;10m-1[0m cast to [38;5;10mchar[0m).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mvector.rs[22m - Generic dynamic array storing raw bytes with element size tracking. Supports push/pop/peek with index management, save/restore state, shift operations, and cloning. Uses [38;5;10mVectorSave[0m struct for state persistence.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mtoken.rs[22m - Token type checking functions. Faithfully replicates the C bug in [38;5;10mtoken_is_keyword[0m where [38;5;10m=[0m (assignment) is used instead of [38;5;10m==[0m (comparison).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mnode.rs[22m - AST node management using global [38;5;10mMutex<Vec<Node>>[0m storage. Nodes are stored by index (encoded as [38;5;10mu64[0m LE bytes) in vectors. Supports push/pop/peek with root vector tracking.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mlex_process.rs[22m - Lexer process creation with function pointer table for character I/O, token vector allocation, and compiler reference.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mlexer.rs[22m - Full lexical analyzer supporting numbers (decimal, hex, binary), strings, operators (single and compound), symbols, identifiers, keywords, comments (single-line and multi-line), character literals with escape sequences, and expression tracking for parentheses.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mcprocess.rs[22m - Compile process creation that reads files into memory for character-by-character access, with peek/next/push operations.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mparser.rs[22m - Token-to-AST parser that skips newlines/comments and converts NUMBER, IDENTIFIER, and STRING tokens into corresponding AST nodes.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mcompiler.rs[22m - Top-level orchestration: [38;5;10mcompile_file[0m creates a process, runs lexical analysis, then parsing. All wrapper functions delegate to their respective module implementations, with type conversion between the duplicate struct definitions.[0m[0m[38;5;12m[1m✓ Created checkpoint 1

